{"audio": "romans-13.opus", "duration_ms": 134635, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 2080, "end_ms": 3480, "text": "Romans, Chapter Thirteen."}, {"start_ms": 4901, "end_ms": 11261, "text": "Everyone must submit himself to the governing authorities, for there is no authority except that which is from God."}, {"start_ms": 12041, "end_ms": 14662, "text": "The authorities that exist have been appointed by God."}, {"start_ms": 15242, "end_ms": 23223, "text": "Consequently, whoever resists authority is opposing what God has set in place, and those who do so will bring judgment on themselves."}, {"start_ms": 23963, "end_ms": 27523, "text": "For rulers are not a terror to good conduct, but to bad."}, {"start_ms": 28103, "end_ms": 30483, "text": "Do you want to be unafraid of the one in authority?"}, {"start_ms": 30923, "end_ms": 33464, "text": "Then do what is right, and you will have his approval."}, {"start_ms": 33924, "end_ms": 36204, "text": "For he is God’s servant for your good."}, {"start_ms": 36864, "end_ms": 40705, "text": "But if you do wrong, be afraid, for he does not carry the sword in vain."}, {"start_ms": 41225, "end_ms": 44925, "text": "He is God’s servant, an agent of retribution to the wrongdoer."}, {"start_ms": 45885, "end_ms": 52726, "text": "Therefore it is necessary to submit to authority, not only to avoid punishment, but also as a matter of conscience."}, {"start_ms": 53306, "end_ms": 55246, "text": "This is also why you pay taxes."}, {"start_ms": 55766, "end_ms": 59267, "text": "For the authorities are God’s servants, who devote themselves to their work."}, {"start_ms": 59707, "end_ms": 70548, "text": "Pay everyone what you owe him: taxes to whom taxes are due, revenue to whom revenue is due, respect to whom respect is due, honor to whom honor is due."}, {"start_ms": 71148, "end_ms": 74628, "text": "Be indebted to no one, except to one another in love."}, {"start_ms": 75148, "end_ms": 77709, "text": "For he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law."}, {"start_ms": 78329, "end_ms": 93150, "text": "The commandments “Do not commit adultery,” “Do not murder,” “Do not steal,” “Do not covet,” and any other commandments, are summed up in this one decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.” Love does no wrong to its neighbor."}, {"start_ms": 93550, "end_ms": 96071, "text": "Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law."}, {"start_ms": 97231, "end_ms": 99811, "text": "And do this, understanding the occasion."}, {"start_ms": 100411, "end_ms": 106992, "text": "The hour has come for you to wake up from your slumber, for our salvation is nearer now than when we first believed."}, {"start_ms": 107632, "end_ms": 110732, "text": "The night is nearly over; the day has drawn near."}, {"start_ms": 111372, "end_ms": 115433, "text": "So let us lay aside the deeds of darkness and put on the armor of light."}, {"start_ms": 115893, "end_ms": 125994, "text": "Let us behave decently, as in the daytime, not in carousing and drunkenness, not in sexual immorality and debauchery, not in dissension and jealousy."}, {"start_ms": 126794, "end_ms": 133095, "text": "Instead, clothe yourselves with the Lord Jesus Christ, and make no provision for the desires of the flesh."}], "words": [{"t": "Romans,", "s": 2080, "e": 2540, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 2640, "e": 2960, "si": 0}, {"t": "Thirteen.", "s": 3000, "e": 3480, "si": 0}, {"t": "Everyone", "s": 4901, "e": 5381, "si": 1}, {"t": "must", "s": 5461, "e": 5721, "si": 1}, {"t": "submit", "s": 5801, "e": 6081, "si": 1}, {"t": "himself", "s": 6121, "e": 6541, "si": 1}, {"t": "to", "s": 6621, "e": 6701, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 6741, "e": 6821, "si": 1}, {"t": "governing", "s": 6861, "e": 7201, "si": 1}, {"t": "authorities,", "s": 7241, "e": 7841, "si": 1}, {"t": "for", "s": 7941, "e": 8061, "si": 1}, {"t": "there", "s": 8121, "e": 8321, "si": 1}, {"t": "is", "s": 8421, "e": 8581, "si": 1}, {"t": "no", "s": 8701, "e": 8781, "si": 1}, {"t": "authority", "s": 8901, "e": 9321, "si": 1}, {"t": "excep